cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: shared-memories-for-agents
abstract: >-
  Implementation of shared memories for LLM-based web agents: a LangGraph
  Observe-Think-Act loop that writes per-user private memories, then an
  InvisibleInk pipeline that releases a shared store under differential
  privacy, evaluated on WebArena.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
authors:
  - family-names: Frizlen
    given-names: Yasmine
    affiliation: University of Essex
keywords:
  - differential privacy
  - LLM agents
  - agent memory
  - WebArena
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      InvisibleInk: High-Utility and Low-Cost Text Generation with
      Differential Privacy
    authors:
      - family-names: Vinod
        given-names: Vishnu
      - family-names: Pillutla
        given-names: Krishna
      - family-names: Guha Thakurta
        given-names: Abhradeep
    collection-title: Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems
    year: 2025
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: arXiv:2507.02974
    notes: >-
      Algorithm 1 is the basis of the differentially private generation in
      src/agent_memories/agent/invisible_ink/. The authors' invink package
      supplies the difference clipping, Top-k+ and zCDP accounting
      primitives.
